  "problem": "Find the converse of the following statement: \n\n$\\,$ **If** $\\pi \\in Z,$ **then** $7$ is composite.",
  "worked_solution": "In our conditional statement:\n\n- The antecedent is $A:$ $\\pi \\in Z.$\n\n- The consequent is $B:$ $7$ is composite.\n\nThe converse of a conditional statement $A\u21d2B$ is given by \n\n$$\nB\u21d2A.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the converse is the following: \n\n$\\,$ If $7$ is composite, then $\\pi \\in Z.$",
